  "releaseNotes": "- Adds standard AI SDK source and file parts to conversation and published API\n  responses while preserving existing text, segments, events and business results\n- Displays compact source references with direct HTTP(S) originals, safe MCP\n  resource icons, document filenames and a lightweight notice for private sources\n- Keeps the source footer name-only, without a heading count or per-row numbers;\n  inline citations retain their small numbered markers\n- Unifies search, page-open and page-find activity rows across Codex and OpenCode,\n  with truthful execution states, original targets and single-line truncation\n- Bounds public source metadata before validation, preserves ordinary author\n  query parameters while rejecting credential-bearing links, and retains text\n  when legacy message segments contain only sources\n- Aligns TypeScript SDK source-icon types with Core and shares citation URI\n  normalization without introducing new runtime dependencies\n- Reuses Runtime `1.0.0-beta.26`; configuration, credentials, conversations,\n  attachments, Skills and durable workspace data remain outside Core releases",
